WEBVTT

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.980
Music King here to announce a special 
performance by hip newcomers to the scene!

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.360
In NO Hurry to Shout is finally 
making an appearance!

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.240
The Mysterious Eyepatched and Masked Band

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.990
Oh, hey, it's In NO Hurry.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.120
The other day, I spotted a 
childhood friend of mine at school.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.790
You mean Nino-chan?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.330
I'm surprised you remembered her name.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.920
I remember everything you say.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.120
You're scaring me.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.930
Aw, don't praise me so much.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.560
So? Did you say anything to her?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.640
No. I didn't talk to her, 
and I plan to keep it that way.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.940
I'm in the advanced class, so we're 
not even in the same building.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.480
Why won't you talk to her?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.280
I'm sure if I met her, I wouldn't be 
able to compose music anymore.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.240
<i>They keep everything about them hidden, 
from their identities to their profiles.</i>

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.620
<i>In No Hurry, or In No Hurry to Shout, the band 
that hides behind masks and eyepatches.</i>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.060
I thought they'd absolutely never appear on TV.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.580
<i>After the turmoil over their breakup, 
they're back for their TV debut!</i>

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.040
<i>Look forward to it!</i>

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.970
♭03 Whatever It Takes, Right Now

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.120
<i>After singing for six years,</i>

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.480
<i>I finally found Yuzu.</i>

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:57.210
<i>But I haven't reached Momo at all.</i>

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.710
You'll see him again.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.420
<i>Is it enough to just keep singing like I have?</i>

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.370
<i>Will that reach him?</i>

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.250
That was In NO Hurry, wasn't it?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.370
It was "High School," for sure.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.160
Now I want to listen to it.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.670
Me, too.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.880
<i>In NO Hurry's songs are reaching everyone.</i>

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:28.120
<i>But my song won't work as a guide yet.</i>

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.890
<i>That's right. It's just not enough.</i>

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.270
<i>There's something lacking in my song.</i>

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.730
Light Music Club

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.440
I'm quitting as your vocalist.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.950
Huh?!

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.960
Well, having me around isn't 
going to help Yuzu write music.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.820
He could only write before because 
he thought of me as Arisugawa Nino.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.030
Th-That's not how it was at all!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.080
Exactly right

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.080
Yuzu-kun, check your forehead.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.660
I hate lies.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.090
As time went by, you could write less and less.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:01.670
But as soon as you met Alice again, 
you could write perfectly fine again.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.590
Yuzu, you can write music again?

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.680
You never told us that, Yuzu-kun!

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.680
And you want me to keep this up, 
knowing I'm not good enough?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.440
I can't do that!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.190
Um, excuse me. I have something 
I'd like to ask you.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:20.940
What?!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.980
Stay away from here! You suck at singing!

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.960
Oh, no! Don't tell me we've 
got a catfight on our hands!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.830
So? What are you gonna do, Yuzu-kun?

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.920
There's the topic of disbanding, too.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.060
We'll talk through everything 
with Yana tomorrow.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.550
Mushroom-san!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.430
Mushroom?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.980
Do I suck at singing?

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:48.680
What?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.030
I want to know!

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:50.030
Too close!

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.930
You're the only one close to me that 
I know of who sings, Mushroom-san!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.400
Stop calling me Mushroom! 
My name's Suguri Miou.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.520
Please tell me, Suguri-san.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.070
What does my singing lack?

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.570
What? You're so pushy.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.620
If you want me to tell you if you're 
good or bad, you're not good.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.370
But you have an interesting voice with impact, 
so there are probably those who'd like you.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.420
Does that mean it can't reach far?

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.520
What do I need to change?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.010
You don't need to change anything, really.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.120
No, I do!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.760
I want to change my voice into something 
that'll reach everyone around the globe.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.350
I want it to reach the person I like.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:37.240
Th-The person you like?! Don't tell 
me he's a tiny milk addict!

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.900
No, he's an austere person with 
glasses and a sense of dignity.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.100
What? So he's a forty-something?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.090
He's my age.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.320
What kind of first-year is that?

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:48.000
I haven't heard from him in six years.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.160
But he told me we can use my song 
as a guide to find each other again.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.410
That's why I sing.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.060
Huh? That's totally out there.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.630
Even so, I want to do everything I can.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.130
If I'm lacking something, I want to fix that.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:08.970
Come with me.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.580
I'll take you down a notch or two.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.020
Abdominal respiration.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.760
What you lack is the basics.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.080
You're completely reckless.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.040
You're way down at the 
very bottom of everything.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.000
<i>I'm at the bottom of everything?</i>

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.650
But it's frustrating how much 
you draw people to you.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.510
Teach me abdominal respiration, Suguri-san!

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.300
Huh?! Wait...

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:50.800
In other words...

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:52.430
In other words,

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:55.260
I just have to crawl my way to the top!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.520
Right...

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.660
<i>I'll find out everything I'm lacking,</i>

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.960
<i>learn everything I can,</i>

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.410
<i>and take off from there.</i>

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.420
<i>Anything I can do to get just a little higher.</i>

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:17.830
How did I get stuck doing this?

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:23.010
But it's been a while since 
I've practiced this much.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.670
You were just lacking so much,

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.350
I was almost ready to give up.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.990
Suguri-san, you're amazing.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:36.240
You know exactly where you 
belong, and what you're lacking.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.760
If I had that, I could take action right now.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.490
Thank you, Suguri-san.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.860
I'll definitely get better.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:53.740
I'm not going to lose either, Nino.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.120
Got it, Miou.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.670
<i>I want to get better.</i>

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:03.290
<i>This is the first time I've felt this way.</i>

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.870
Voice Training

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.260
Yuzu.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.760
<i>Abdominal respiration.</i>

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.920
<i>Abdominal respiration.</i>

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:26.860
Yuzu!

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:29.020
It reached him.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.280
It reached him!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:37.160
Yuzu! Yuzu! Yuzu! Yuzu! Yuzu!

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.160
Shut up!

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.550
<i>I'll make it reach even further,</i>

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.710
<i>until it can reach Momo. For sure.</i>

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:54.650
Jeez, what was that all about? 
Yelling my name five times in a row...

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.690
Well, if it isn't Eyelashes.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:04.520
You take this train, too?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.230
Don't call me Eyelashes! 
I told you, I'm Yuzuriha!

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.400
I'm going to Kamakura.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.270
I'm going to North Kamakura, Lash.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:16.280
Don't shorten it. 
Fine, just call me Eyelashes.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.410
Thanks. You're pretty nice, Eyelashes.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.540
Sakaki, you're a real weirdo, aren't you?

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.250
Am I?

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.590
What's so funny, Eyelashes?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.630
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:36.140
<i>So, for our third week, we'll have the 
TV debut of In NO Hurry to Shout!</i>

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.430
<i>And they'll perform their 
highly anticipated new single!</i>

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.720
<i>Look forward to it!</i>

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.270
I wonder what their new song will be like.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.400
<i>Now, we'll end this week's show with this song!</i>

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.940
Namimachi Berry Baby

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.940
Lyrics: Kuze Tsukika  Composition: Kiryuu Momo

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:52.940
Kiryuu... Momo!

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:56.450
<i>Kiryuu... Isn't that Momo's 
mother's maiden name?</i>

00:09:57.190 --> 00:10:00.620
<i>Composition? Don't tell me...</i>

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.120
Profile

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.120
Kiryuu Momo 
Sex: Male 
Blood Type: AB

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.490
<i>The same sex and blood type as my Momo.</i>

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:11.290
I'd like to meet Kiryuu Momo-san.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.240
O-Only people affiliated with 
our company may see him.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.750
Then can you at least tell me 
what kind of person he is?!

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:19.030
I don't know myself.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:28.440
Vocalist Audition 
Be produced by Kiryuu Momo

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.800
<i>Applicants may choose any song.</i>

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.440
<i>The successful candidate will be the main 
vocalist of a band set to debut this summer.</i>

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:32.520
If I make it through that audition, 
will I be able to meet Kiryuu Momo?!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.880
Huh? Well, yes.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.440
Thanks for everything!

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.010
<i>I'm going to apply for that audition.</i>

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.950
<i>If I make it through the screening,</i>

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.820
<i>I'll be able to see whether 
Kiryuu Momo is my Momo or not!</i>

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.030
Is this...

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.000
Let's make Arisugawa Nino the new vocalist.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.430
I'm the one who recommended her.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:04.850
Her voice has the best 
kind of impact you'll need

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.150
to make your presence known 
in the major scene.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:11.120
Yuzu, it's up to you, but—

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.030
No!

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:16.340
Didn't I tell you I want to quit?

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.400
So why are things going in this direction?

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.910
There's absolutely no way.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.740
I don't get him.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.760
Why is he so against it?

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:33.790
Didn't he put this band together 
in the first place for her?

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.050
Yuzu just doesn't

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:39.480
want anyone else to know about his voice.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.570
<i>Worn-out smiles</i>

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.350
<i>In the prison prepared by adults</i>

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.070
<i>Under the dark sky</i>

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:51.570
<i>When I stretch out my hand</i>

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:53.810
<i>You slip and fall</i>

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:57.180
<i>You wrench open your falling eyelids</i>

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.800
Believe you'll reach him and keep singing.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:02.070
<i>When I say, "Look at me"</i>

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.070
I'm sure you'll see him.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.850
<i>It's because of his words and his song</i>

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:09.290
<i>These unrequited feelings will never change</i>

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.290
<i>that I've been able to keep 
on going without hesitating.</i>

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:13.920
<i>Just let everything go, far out into the sky</i>

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:18.810
<i>Shout out! This song 
is the melody inside you</i>

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:17.920
Damn it. She's just the best.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:23.970
<i>Overflowing with all your 
love, wishes, and lies</i>

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.560
Why?

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.230
<i>Shout out!</i>

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:26.970
<i>I'm hiding—</i>

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:34.400
It took me until morning 
to finish writing my résumé.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.120
"Be Produced by Kiryuu Momo! Vocal Audition" Entry

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.120
Send

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.360
Sending!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.740
Your entry has been sent.
Thank you for your application.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.030
Please let me be accepted!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.290
I'd better report to Yuzu, too!

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.040
This is bad.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:55.620
I can't stop.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.340
I'm overflowing.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:02.670
Well, of course. I've always...

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:07.310
I've always written songs because 
I wanted Alice to sing them.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.310
Kanade?

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.600
Are you still sleeping? 
You're going to be late.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.440
I-I'm awake! I'll be fine!

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.260
Yuzu, shocking news flash.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.010
Too close!

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.510
I found someone who may be Momo!

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.840
He's a composer.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:58.520
Have you heard of Kiryuu Momo?

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.180
I have.

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:07.480
He's holding an audition where he'll 
produce the winner, so I applied.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.910
If I make it through, 
I might be able to meet him.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.290
Momo's a composer?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.930
Oh, well, Kiryuu Momo is.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.450
I still don't know if he's 
the real Momo or not yet.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.560
Huh? I thought you'd be happy for me.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.160
If you get accepted, are you 
going to sing Momo's songs?

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:31.180
Oh, I never thought about 
what I'd do if I got accepted.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:33.430
But that's right. I guess that's what—

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.060
No!

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.560
It's nothing.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.350
Yuzu, what's the matter?

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.380
I said it's nothing.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:46.480
Yuzu!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.030
I just can't accept this.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:55.040
After all, it was Arisugawa Nino's fault 
that Yuzu lost his ability to sing.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:00.960
If he hadn't sung for her six years ago,

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.460
he might have recovered enough 
to be able to sing now.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.070
<i>What? Wait...</i>

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.520
I won't sing.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.010
<i>Wait.</i>

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.310
I'll turn into foam and disappear.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:21.330
<i>Wait!</i>

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:42.680
He's lying.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:47.210
What Haruyoshi said is a lie, okay?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.720
<i>Wait... Wait. Wait!</i>

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:54.850
I can sing... just fine.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.760
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:59.540
<i>He told me he wouldn't sing.</i>

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.480
<i>He would never sing.</i>

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:04.930
<i>But that one time...</i>

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.890
<i>Just that one time, when he tried to stop me...</i>

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.230
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.360
<i>The week after he sang with me...</i>

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:16.480
<i>Yuzu disappeared.</i>

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:20.250
Yuzu... Yuzu!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.540
Shut up! I can sing!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.500
Just watch!

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.610
<i>It's that song.</i>

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.500
<i>He's trying to sing it.</i>

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:50.650
<i>Yuzu!</i>

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.640
I can sing, okay?

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.330
I can... sing.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.810
Yuzu...

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:02.540
I'm just not feeling well today!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:07.170
<i>It's because I screamed back then.</i>

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:07.750
<i>That's why...</i>

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.630
You're wrong! It's not your fault.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:17.690
I didn't sing back then just to
see this look on your face.

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:22.070
I just wanted you to keep singing forever.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:27.670
So you'd better not ever worry about it.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:33.950
Never, ever worry about it.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:37.650
Just sing.

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:05.880
I found it.

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:08.820
My voice.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:17.140
Six years ago, I was hospitalized 
due to an illness in my throat.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:22.590
I used to like writing 
songs and singing them.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:26.890
But I was told to never sing 
again once I was hospitalized.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.280
That's why I snuck out on Wednesdays,

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.370
and wrote music as large as 
I could on Yuigahama Beach.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.350
It was my way of venting my anger.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.420
And that's when I heard you sing.

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:43.390
I thought I had found the voice I had lost.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:19.640
After singing with you, I was 
transferred to a hospital in Tokyo.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:25.760
But I wanted so much for you 
to sing that song until the end.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:30.140
So I snuck out just one 
more day and wrote it.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:37.610
Before the concert we did together, 
when you sang that melody,

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.190
I was really happy.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:45.910
I thought you were singing 
my song, just like always.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:55.670
Alice, I want you to keep singing—

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:56.670
I can't!

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:58.560
I'm sorry, Yuzu.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:20.310
<i>I'm the one who should 
be saying sorry, Alice.</i>

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.160
<i>I'm the one who tore up your heart.</i>

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:31.670
<i>But that moment when you 
learned everything...</i>

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.340
<i>One of the dreams I've always 
hoped would come true</i>

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:47.830
<i>finally came true.</i>

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:58.090
You sang for me.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:02.410
For the first time,

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:07.550
you sang only for me.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.830
Tsukika-san, what's the meaning of this?

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:17.540
You let her in because you 
knew she was Nino, didn't you?

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.090
Oh, so that really is Nino-chan.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.090
I'll be blunt. I didn't let her in 
because she was Nino-chan.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.400
You know, that girl

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:32.960
recorded by the sea or something. 
The sound of waves was overwhelming.

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:36.350
Not only that, she recorded with her phone, 
so the sound quality is awful.

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:41.780
But she had a voice that was far 
more memorable than anyone else's.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:52.280
<i>I don't have anything to hide 
or be scared of anymore.</i>

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.650
<i>I want to steal you from Momo.</i>

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:11.060
I'll tell Alice

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:09.060
<i>Whatever it takes.</i>

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:11.360
<i>Right now.</i>

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:16.940
that I want her to be the 
vocalist of In NO Hurry.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:52.280
♭04 That Day, We Who Were Hiding 
How We Truly Felt Joined Hands
